      "title": "Stages of Chronic Kidney Disease",
      "text": "[TABLE: Stages of Chronic Kidney Disease]\nClinical Facts:\n- Stage 1: Kidney damage with normal or increased GFR (≥90 mL/min/1.73 m²)\n- Stage 2: Kidney damage with mild decreased GFR (60-89 mL/min/1.73 m²)\n- Stage 3: Moderate decreased GFR (30-59 mL/min/1.73 m²)\n- Stage 4: Severe decreased GFR (15-29 mL/min/1.73 m²)\n- Stage 5: Kidney failure (<15 mL/min or dialysis)\nClinical Relationships:\n- Chronic Kidney Disease -> [defines] -> Stages of CKD",
