      "title": "Stages of Chronic Kidney Disease: A Clinical Action Plan",
      "text": "[TABLE: Stages of Chronic Kidney Disease: A Clinical Action Plan]\nClinical Facts:\n- Stage 1: GFR > 90 mL/min/1.73 m² - Diagnosis and treatment, treatment of comorbid conditions, slowing progression.\n- Stage 2: GFR 60-89 mL/min/1.73 m² - Estimating progression.\n- Stage 3: GFR 30-59 mL/min/1.73 m² - Evaluating and managing complications.\n- Stage 4: GFR 15-29 mL/min/1.73 m² - Preparation for kidney replacement therapy.\n- Stage 5: GFR < 15 mL/min/1.73 m² - Replacement (if symptoms present).\nClinical Relationships:\n- Chronic kidney disease -> [defines] -> kidney damage or GFR < 60 mL/min/1.73 m² for 3 months",
